  "worked_solution": "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=25\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 25\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{25\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2r=2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=5\\,\\text{mm}.\n$$",
